-- title:
--   Units on Ω are pinned between two adjacent vertices
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, with fraction field $K_0$, let $\varpi \in R$ be irreducible and suppose the residue ring $R/(\varpi)$ is finite. Let $K$ be a field extension of $K_0$ carrying a valuation $v$ with values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero $\Gamma_0$, complete and algebraically closed. Assume: $v(a) \le 1$ for every $a \in R$ (hypothesis `hint`); conversely every $a \in K_0$ with $v(a) \le 1$ lies in the image of $R$ (hypothesis `hv`); the powers of $v(\varpi)$ are coinitial in $\Gamma_0$, i.e. for each $\varepsilon \neq 0$ some $v(\varpi)^N \le \varepsilon$ (hypothesis `hq`); and the rank-one condition `hrk`, that for $x$ with $v(x) < 1$ and $y \neq 0$ some power $v(x)^n \le v(y)$. Let $\varpi_1$ be a pseudo-uniformiser, i.e. an element of $K_0$ with $0 < v(\varpi_1) < 1$ such that for every $a \in K_0^\times$ there is $N$ with $v(\varpi_1)^N \le v(a) \le v(\varpi_1)^{-N}$, and assume `IsExhausted` for $\varpi_1$: every point of $\Omega = K \setminus \mathrm{im}(K_0 \to K)$ lies in one of the affinoids $\mathrm{affinoid}\ \varpi_1\ n$. Let $f$ be an element of the ring `holRing` of functions $\Omega \to K$ whose restriction to each affinoid of level $n$ is a uniform limit of rational functions without poles there, with values uniformly bounded; assume $f$ is a unit of that ring. Then for every $z \in \Omega$ there exist $g, g' \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, points $w, w'$ in the level-$0$ affinoid (those $w$ with $v(w) \le 1$ and $v(w - a) \ge 1$ for all $a \in K_0$ with $v(a) \le 1$) and points $y, y' \in \Omega$ with $y = g \cdot w$ and $y' = g' \cdot w'$ for the Möbius action of the classes of $g, g'$ in $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ on $\mathbb{P}^1(K)$ read affinely, such that the vertices $g \cdot v_0$ and $g' \cdot v_0$ are adjacent in the Bruhat–Tits tree — the simple graph on homothety classes of full $R$-lattices in $K^2$ generated by the adjacency relation on lattices, $v_0$ being the class of the standard lattice — and
--   $$\min\bigl(v(f(y)), v(f(y'))\bigr) \le v(f(z)) \le \max\bigl(v(f(y)), v(f(y'))\bigr).$$
--
--   This is the statement that the valuation of an invertible rigid function on Drinfeld's upper half plane at an arbitrary point is squeezed between its values at two points lying over the endpoints of a single edge of the Bruhat–Tits tree, reflecting the monotonicity of $\log|f|$ along edges under the reduction map $\Omega \to \mathcal{T}$. It is used in the construction of theta functions and period data for Mumford quotients, notably in the results on uniformisation of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ and on the period pairing.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_Omega_exists_adj_min_le_v_apply_le_max_of_isUnit.lean

